  "body": "Upgrade workholding and standing-steel collision checks from one rotary axis to a stacked two-axis `(A, C)` trunnion chain.\n\n### Context\n- `Workholding` in `crates/sim/src/verify/workholding.rs` holds only one `Option<RotaryAxis>`.\n- `rotary_axis_of` in `crates/app/src/fixture.rs` sets that axis only for `RotaryContour`, `RotaryParallel`, and `RotaryOffset`, not for 5-axis finishing or two-rotary trunnions.\n- `crates/app/src/posting_swing_standing.rs` reports standing steel as `\"not judged\"` whenever two rotaries turn the work, and `crates/app/src/posting_index_swing.rs` assumes the WCS origin sits at rotary intersection.\n- Depends on schema (#1962) and AC IK solver (#1965).\n\n### Requirements\n- Replace or extend `Workholding::axis` with a general kinematic chain of turning rotaries and offsets matching the `.mch` tree and post-IK `(A, C)` trajectory.\n- Transform fixed fixtures (table, trunnion bridge, stanchions) and turning fixtures (platter, chuck, part) accurately in `posed_steel.rs` across cuts, rapids, and safe-Z rotary unwinds.\n- Check standing-steel clearance in `posting_swing_standing.rs` and `posting_index_swing.rs` using the real `(A, C)` pivot positions instead of assuming zero offset.\n\nDone means: Collision tests verify that fixed-table and trunnion-frame strikes during simultaneous cuts or rapid reorientations block posting by name rather than reporting `\"not judged\"`.\n\nPart of #1958\n",
